    "reading": "The metal main effect is real signal and explains 3.4% of within-cohort variance, which is a lower bound on the explainable share. In R2 terms the ceiling is not identified: pooled replicate sigma is 0.2114 but its median is 0.0265, and only 3 of 848 evaluation cells have a replicate, so the R2 ceiling ranges from 0 to 99.2%. The ranking metrics are far more noise-robust than R2: across the whole plausible noise range sigma in [0.027, 0.36], a perfect predictor of the true cell mean scores top-1 0.70-0.95 and regret 0.001-0.106, always better than the current 0.566 / 0.1186. The break-even noise is sigma>=1.2393 for top-1 and sigma>=0.3948 for regret, both above every defensible estimate. Conclusion: the data is not the binding constraint on the decision layer; the model is.",
